## Numerical formula alignment

Coverage is all seven chapters. I used the supplied measurements and did not re-estimate them. Method: `editions/monroe-1.3/tools/formula_metrics.py`; it strips H1s and marked breaks, excludes fenced notices from sentence/readability statistics while counting their words, treats each non-empty prose line as a paragraph, tokenizes sentences at terminal punctuation followed by a capital/opening quote or paragraph end, and estimates syllables by vowel groups with silent-e/-le adjustments. Proper names and system terms can bias the readability figures. Paragraph/scene targets remain ASR-derived directional proxies.

| Measure | Target / working range | Observed | Assessment |
|---|---:|---:|---|
| Prose words | — | 35,766 (35,792 including 26 notice words) | Near the 38,000 movement budget; no evidence of scene compression. |
| Sentence mean | 14.6 / 13–15.5 | 13.55 | Inside the working range, below the exact target. |
| Sentence median | 11 | 9 | Shorter than target. |
| Sentence population SD | about 26 | 11.6 | Material narrowing of the requested wide distribution. |
| Sentences ≤5 words | 27.7% / up to about 34% | 29.5% | Aligned. Short dialogue is doing legitimate work. |
| Sentences ≥40 words | 3.3% / 2.5–4.5% | 4.1% | Inside the working range. |
| Paragraph mean / median | 26.8 / 18; median up to about 30 | 34.89 / 24 | Median is accepted; mean remains long against the directional proxy. |
| Marked scene breaks per 10k | about 8.7 | 8.38 | Close. |
| Words per scene | about 950 / 850–1,050 | 967.4 | Strong alignment. |
| Flesch Reading Ease | 72.3 | 95.0 | Large drift toward very easy surface prose. |
| Flesch-Kincaid grade | 6.8 / 3.5–6 | 3.37 | Just below the accepted floor and far below the exact target. |

The three primary working-range checks pass: mean sentence length, ≥40-word share, and words per scene. Short-sentence share and paragraph median also remain within accepted drift. The material formula departures are the much narrower sentence spread, median of 9 rather than 11, and readability far easier than the selected target. The prose itself is not childish—its ethics, tactics, and interiority are sophisticated—so the readability result likely reflects short, low-syllable vocabulary as much as conceptual simplicity. It remains a measured miss and should not be hidden.

A formula repair should be selective and sentence-led, never scripted: join only adjacent short declaratives that are one thought, allow more clear 12–25-word syntax in exposition/interiority, and choose precise vocabulary where it is already natural. Do not pad dialogue, alter protected wording, or shorten the Ring/deep reading. Chasing FRE by swapping in ornate words would damage the thirteen-year-old standard without fixing rhythm.

### Formula items not supplied as reproducible counts

- **Progression density:** UNMEASURED. No project-specific lexicon count was supplied, so compliance with ≈42 hits per 10k cannot be assigned numerically. Qualitatively, progression language recedes through the recovery and spikes at the acquisition as planned.
- **Development beats:** no precise count assigned. Manually identified beats are well distributed across all six: Cael releases the full suite and later admits what he wants; Lira keeps both the arm order and “Later”; Brom becomes the arms and then lets another man make his bread; Karis spends her reserve and restrains her questions; Seln rejects being used as an excuse and opens the map-memory drawer; Oryn adds a stop and tests the line eight times for herself.
