editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:125:- **Seln's locked case:** the cache. He brought it east in his own post satchel; since the shelf it rides under the cart's canvas with the three boxes (edition B6 ch60). Once the cart is sold in Lowmarch's first week (#23) it goes back on its strap and is on him on every road. **Never opened in this book.** [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: coordinator ruling]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:126:- **The cart and the horse** (edition B6 ch56, ch60). **C1 default:** sold in Lowmarch's first week. The sale and the rest of the B6 purse become a sealed reserve the crew does not live on. The log's "in hand" counts only the board purse. OWNER #23 governs: sell cart and gelding in Lowmarch's first week; put the sale and remaining Book 6 purse into a sealed reserve the crew does not live on. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit D3, N7]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:129:- **Money at entry:** the board purse is empty (nothing earned). The Book 6 purse is as C1 rules.
