editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:196:- **#23 executed on the page:** the gelding went to the ferryman and the cart to the smith in Lowmarch's first week; the sale and the rest of the Book 6 purse are sewn and waxed into a reserve under five thumbprints at the bottom of the third box. "In hand" never counts the reserve.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:202:- **Protected text:** every §10 unit for source chapters 1–2 is placed once and exact, including the #48 reconciled wordings and the first pole with "Since my Kindling". Pike's Thornwater document is quoted once (ch6); ch7 refers to it in narration.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:216:- **The sale (#23; flag):** the gelding to the ferryman, for his capstan, with dry room for the three boxes in the loft over the drum as part of the price; the old capstan mule put out to grass. The cart to the smith, who means to cut its axle to mule gauge and hire it out. Brom's bill-hook came under the cart's seat board. Lira's long knife is the last thing the Book 6 purse buys. No figure is given for the sale, the purse or the reserve.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:238:**Cael.** Eighteen, said to Pike on day 9. **Nine confirmed fragments and the uncounted anomaly** (*Still open. Still real. Patience.*, written on day 18). **Deployment since the Line: none.** No injury; the forearm is "sound again" by day 5 and is not mentioned afterward. Idle states: Shadow sealed, costing from waking, drifting at dusk (two drifts, logged as rent); Anchor asking at every sill, gate, rim and rail; Blade asking *Edge?* and taking names; Storm heavy; Wind leaning his feet. He has not read the Iron read once. The log has an entry for most days, each ending on the deployment line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:244:**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three. Uninjured. Sets no points on a road. Holds: the field archive; a leaf headed *stillhound*, underlined once, with five counts and *110 yards* (*gate to stone; C.'s count, paced at a yard to the stride; not taped*); the entry of her own not-asking (day 22); the five column heads with *Outcome* underlined twice; Pike's copied line; **the carter's map**. She has asked nobody what the animal is waiting for.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:257:Movement 2 must inherit these surviving-prose facts in addition to its own explicit entry paragraph:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:263:- **Asset state after #23:** no cart or horse; the reserve is sealed under masonry chips in the third box and opens only by all five; the boxes lodge over the ferry drum when the crew is near Lowmarch; Seln's closed case is back on its strap (`manuscript/chapter-03.md:107,123-185`; `manuscript/chapter-04.md:277`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:55-65`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:273:## AFTER MOVEMENT 2 — chapters 8–14, days 51–69 past the Line (drafted 2026-10-11, author claude-opus-5-5, NO-SOURCE method)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:325:**Objects and money.** Three boxes over the ferry drum. The reserve unopened. Board purse: **sixty-two marks earned** (18 + ford 40 + well 4); **fifty-two in hand** (one mark on flour and bacon on day 51; one to the hold for linen and thread; coppers unitemised). Hesk's satchel holds the log (with the finding and the seal entry), the old volume, the observation notebook, Pike's two lines on bark, and Hesk's letter. Cael's coat has lost its left sleeve. The ash stick is propping an old carter's shaft under the ash.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:348:## AFTER MOVEMENT 3 — chapters 15–22, days 70–84 past the Line (windows to day 92) (drafted 2026-10-11, author claude-opus-5-5, NO-SOURCE method)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:354:- **Oryn** is the first healer met past the Line. Tide as taught: contact only; about three serious mendings a day fed and slept, two on a road; cannot heal herself; "Because I cannot mend what I can't read."; the short reading (seconds) and the long one (both hands, all of her, minutes) — healing houses say surface and deep. The stall is named once. She knows NOTHING of fragments, has run no deep reading, records nothing and remembers. Her reading of Cael stopped at five; she said only "a river in the dark" and that it has no side she can find. "More than one" is NOT said (Movement 5).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:425:- Oryn has failed three surface readings of Cael, knows only that he heals fast with no readable current, knows nothing of fragments, has run no deep reading, keeps no written record, and has put one day on her route for the promised whole-and-still reading (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:317-351`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:53-89,137-155,211-233`). Her mule still carries her panniers and covered crossbow; do not spend owner decision #24 early (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:143-159`; `OWNER-DECISIONS.md:103-107`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:434:## AFTER MOVEMENT 4 — chapters 23–30, days 84–96 past the Line (drafted 2026-10-11, author claude-opus-5-5, NO-SOURCE method)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:437:- **The line (OWNER-pending #49, default in force).** At the line the five live Arbiters stop at the same step: Karis's, Lira's, Brom's, Seln's, Oryn's. Cael's own Arbiter has been dark since his Kindling and nothing in him changes there; his fragments go on answering inside. The protected log entries are word for word (their loose "mine" is his shorthand). Outside them nothing says "his Path", nothing says his Arbiter is awake or unaffected, and nothing says WHY the fragments answer. The word *Quieting* has not been said. "Compact" has not been said aloud: the stake carries the registry stamp. "Made" has been said of the place once, by Karis.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:439:- **Ring geometry — the manuscript governs (Movement 5 inherits):** the western line stone is 220 yards from the floor's middle; the floor is 26 of Cael's yard-strides across; the den is under the floor's EASTERN lip; so den to the western line is about 233 yards and den to the eastern perimeter about 207. The protected round is 1,374 yards and a piece (sixty-two cords and twenty strides); radius ten cords; the constant offset is six and a half feet per cord. NO cord length and NO stride length is stated, and none is to be added. "A hundred and fifty yards inside" is dropped from the plan.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:441:- **The trials at the line** ran Karis, Brom, Seln, Lira, Oryn. Lira's full burst became one step; her words on stepping back out are the protected clock line. Oryn has crossed twice (with Brom; with the six) and reads nobody inside; her eight solo crossings are Movement 5's. Seln's map memory is Movement 5's.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:464:- **The registry's printed sheet (flag):** east of the Line it shows a river or two without their bends, hills drawn alike, and seven dashed roads with no names that run out into white and stop; the third from the top crosses the first water (no ferry, no Lowmarch) and ends three fingers east of it, at about Thornwater's fence or an hour beyond. **"Void"** (flag): Seln says that in a registry's usage an entry is void when nothing is written against it, and supposes that a carter was once shown such a sheet.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:485:**Cael.** Eighteen. **Nine confirmed fragments and the uncounted anomaly.** Logged deployment since the Line: one (the ford); the day-96 entry carries no deployment line. **On the 96th, unwitnessed:** the Iron read opened a pace short of the line and carried across it; a foot's worth of Wind evasion twenty strides inside; the Iron read once more on the floor. Shadow is sealed and untouched; it lifted at dusk on the 95th at the turn of the ruts and on the 96th inside the line, and was refused both times. Anchor asked at the stone and at the stake. Ribs: taped, eighteen days from the break, three to go. Calf: bound in Oryn's linen, closing by itself. He has told nobody that anything answered him inside, and has given Karis "It was dark before… It's dark now." for her sixth row. Hesk's satchel holds the log, the old volume, the notebook, Hesk's letter, Pike's lines on bark, and now Ephram's letter and Vell's. He has not answered any of the three.
