editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md-143-## 47. Book 6 ch49 — the certification minute's "evaluator of record" (coordinator ruling, 2026-10-11)
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md-144-The protected Tier B minute reads "*Evaluation-protocol certification: declined by the evaluator of record; proceeding on the presiding seat's authority.*" In this edition Gault is the evaluator of record and the Archmarshal's office is the certifying office that declined. **Ruling: the protected line stays verbatim and is read as the form's own mislabel** — an old column heading with no place for the right office — which the scene already dramatizes (four pens stop; Gault "had declined nothing"). One plain sentence was added outside the protected line so a young reader is told so directly: "The refusal was the Archmarshal's; the form's old column had only Gault's title to put it under." Owner may instead release the protected line and have it name the certifying office.
