   542	### New canon minted (author's list)
   543	- **The pack came home by the west (flag).** Nine came over the floor's western lip at sunset, up the party's own trodden lane, having gone out by the east at first light. Cael notes that a healer counted to ten on a wrist at that stone at noon with her Path running; "he did not know that it bore, and he put it by for whoever kept findings." It is not entered as a finding by anybody.
   544	- **The nine, as seen:** a pale one; a heavy one with a dark stripe from neck to tail; two smaller that keep shoulder to shoulder; one long in the leg; one grey to the eyes; three not told apart. Dead: the pale one (on the floor, four strides in from the western lip, with the bolt in it) and the long-legged one (a yard west of the line stone).
   545	- **The rain-rut (flag):** natural, on the swell's north-west flank; it begins under the floor's north-western lip and runs down a little north of west, knee-deep and a stride wide; abreast of the lane's sixty-yard mark it lies about forty yards north. Nothing made is added to the site.
   546	- **How the hounds behave inside (flag):** careless. They drift; they keep station on the slowest walker; they do not cut a lane that they could cut; one sits down in the lane behind the file. One comes onto a pole a minute after watching another do it. A man who cannot declare is "a man with a stick" to them. A scream turns no head. With their first mover dead, two stand. Once something declares inside, they come as the ford's seven came.
   547	- **The lip in a fight:** a hand's drop spoils a hound's spring, since its hind feet have nothing square to push from on a rolled rim. It gives a bow a rest.
   548	- **Oryn's crossbow (flag):** has an iron stirrup at its nose and is spanned with a hook, which was in the near-side pannier and was not fetched; drawn by hand it cuts the fingers. It "throws low, a hand" at thirteen feet. A leather sleeve on the stock held **six** bolts. No history of the bow is given; Oryn says only that she looked at it at noon and left it, "a healer's reason".
   549	- **Bolts:** one left in the hound on the floor; one cut out of the hound at the stone; **five in the sleeve** from the 97th. Karis keeps the sleeve while Brom may draw nothing.
   550	- **The wall at the line:** nine points and eight joins, sixty yards, the stone in the middle, held for a count of six; "a tenth part left, perhaps". A strip of burnt stems marks it.
   551	- **Storm in a channel:** a lane laid down a rut strips the standing grass of its seed and drives it down the channel; the read cannot be under his soles while a lane is held. Three lanes, with bills of ten, ten and twelve counts.
   552	- **Injuries, as fixed on the page:** Lira, left forearm bitten through between wrist and elbow, held about thirty counts, never shaken; mended in an hour at the line; eight small pink marks; slung in a strip of Thornwater's blanket, the hand under the opposite collarbone. Right ankle over outward a third time; taped on the 97th; flat-footed, whole sole. Karis, throat pressed by her own fists under the jaws; knuckles skinned; no voice on the 96th–97th; a croak on the 98th; single rasped words on the 99th. Brom, a straight cut across four finger-pads of each hand, two of them deep; mended at noon on the 97th; nothing drawn until the hundredth. Cael, left calf opened along the old seam on a stone in the rut; bound by Karis, then by Oryn; counting eleven strides on the 97th, about forty by the evening of the 98th, none by noon of the 99th; a pale seam "four days, counting the one it went on". Left forearm struck in the second lock; dead to the elbow that night; back to the wrist on the 99th. Ribs: the tape off in the yard on the 99th. Seln: nothing. Oryn: spent to the bottom on the 96th; two mendings at noon on the 97th; none on the 98th or 99th.
   553	- **Oryn's rule for the long reading:** unfed, at first light, the door shut; the patient on his back with his head at the stool; a surface count first "so that I'd know I hadn't dreamed it"; her left hand under the nape and her right flat on the breastbone; she talks, "to keep my place". She says twenty minutes beforehand, "near enough".
   554	- **What the reading is like from under it (flag):** it goes along the length of a person and returns to her other hand, at the pace she walks, favouring the right by a hair. He can tell where she is. As she passes: Wind turns over and settles; his palm warms; Compression does nothing; the read wishes to open; the ninth draws itself in small, unasked; the heaviest lies quiet. She says "You're helping." when his neck hardens.
   555	- **How the tenth comes:** an empty place that he had not known of; "a hand held out in the dark" at his breastbone; he opens "the one door in the house that had been shut"; the place fills like a cup; then the lines. He does not try it.
   556	- **Seln's memory (flag):** as a junior he carried a tin with a lead tag from one room to another and counted, without reading, eight fair linen-backed sheets of the country east of the Line: a ruled stroke for the Line, dashed roads carried farther than on the printed sheet, and on some sheets a small round ruled with a compass, empty, with a road going about one; no sign for it in the table at the sheet's foot; one sheet with two. He took them for something guarded. No room, office, year or name is given, and he says that he cannot place the second round.
   557	- **The charcoal ring:** drawn on Karis's thin paper to the carter's measure (three things traced from the hide: the first water, Thornwater's square, a tick to a day; the rest from memory with the paper off the skin). Laid back on the hide it lies on her pencilled ring, a little larger, with one middle. The two rings marked *guess* are not promoted.
   558	- **The posting read as a question:** by Seln, as inference: a paper that sends a crew to fetch what is not there asks only what becomes of the crew; the broker's clerk is to send word west by the next boat.
   559	- **Thornwater:** five on the bench under the back room's window on the 99th, one a man who cut his shin with a scythe "at the start of the harvest"; she reads all five and puts them off until after noon on the 100th. The back room: one window in the eastern wall with a shutter, a bench under it, a scrubbed plank on two trestles, a three-legged stool, a peg on a thong for a latch; her things on a strip of canvas along the sill (tape on its stick, flask, shears, linen, horn cup, bone needle). The bowman takes off his cap when Lira comes in slung.
   560	- **Oryn's route:** "the top gate of my round's eleven days north of here", by the road, at the mule's pace. No lateness figure is given.
   561	- **Karis's page:** a single leaf, two years in the making: a curve for how quickly each fragment came, a column for what each cost afterward, and three words at its head. She calls it a model.
   562	- **Small things:** Karis's lantern holds "three fingers" of oil after the hour and "a finger" in the loft. Seln makes Brom's bread to dictation and it does not burn. One of Thornwater's six blankets is returned a hand narrower. Lira climbs the loft ladder with her right hand and both knees.
   563	
   564	### State at movement end (author; governed by the rulings above and by the surviving prose)
   565	**Calendar.** The morning of the **hundredth day past the Line**, in Thornwater's back room, in the twenty-first minute of the long reading. No season, month or English weekday name is on the page ("first snow", "the snow", "the harvest", "frost"). Days on the page: 96 (sunset to night), 97, 98, 99, 100. Weather: frost every night; a north wind on the Fallow; ice on Thornwater's trough.
   566	
   567	**Where everyone is.** Cael on the plank table with Oryn's hands on him, the door shut. Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln in or about the loft over the barn, with all three boxes and the covenant leaf in Hesk's book. The mule in Thornwater's yard. Five of the hold's people waiting until after noon.
   568	
   569	**Cael.** Eighteen. **Ten confirmed fragments** from the twentieth minute: the tenth is Tide-adjacent, partial, Iron, self and contact, *Acquisition: directed. Engagement: clinical — non-hostile.* It has not been tried, and its cost has not begun. The uncounted anomaly is untouched and unmentioned in this movement. **Deployment since the Line: thirteen** (the ford; twelve in the Ring on the 96th), as his log has it; the noon tests of the 96th are noted in the log as left out. Shadow used **once**. Ribs whole, the tape off on the 99th. Calf closed. Left forearm bruised and working. He has told Oryn two things: that what she saw on the hill was his doing, and, in the last minute, "I need to tell you what I am." He has told nobody why anything answered him inside, and has not told Lira since when he knew. Three letters still unanswered.
   570	
   571	**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. No burst. **Left forearm bitten through on the 96th, mended at the line; slung, and under the order until first snow** (nothing held, struck or caught). **Right ankle over a third time, taped, not mended**; she walks on the whole sole. The new tibia was run on for twenty yards and held. She knows that he chose not to act on the floor and that he had known he could; she has said "Later." and is keeping it. Her long knife is blunt.
   572	
   573	**Brom.** Iron Skin; Copper. Eight finger-pads cut on the string, mended on the 97th; **no string until the hundredth**. He shot twice and killed twice. He carried the middle box through the whole of the Ring. He has the bill; the bow is his to carry and Karis has had the sleeve.
   574	
   575	**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three. **Nine points and eight joins for a count of six at the line on the 96th**; about a tenth left that night; nothing since. Throat mended on the 97th; hoarse single words by the 99th. Holds: eleven Ring sheets, dry, not yet looked at; the box unopened; the carter's map with three rings (two still *guess*) and Seln's charcoal sheet; her leaf *Where / Entered as said / Blank. Stamped. Filed.*; the stub and the entry against herself of the 99th. The two torn leaves lay on the loft's boards. She has asked him nothing.
   576	
   577	**Seln.** Shadow; Bronze. Unmarked. He fetched the bow, opened the jaws, carried Karis to the stone and called "Back". He has said "Compact" aloud once. He has given what he remembers of eight sheets and has refused to guess the file. He has released Cael from keeping the seal as a reason against telling Oryn. **The case is on its strap, on him, shut.**
   578	
   579	**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four. Three mendings on the crew in two days; none since. She has crossed the line eight times alone at dawn on the 98th, which only Cael saw. She has read him five times at the surface and once at depth, and has found movement, "more than one", and no banks. She felt something change in him in the twentieth minute; she has been told that he did it and that he must tell her what he is; **she does not know the mechanism**. Thornwater's bench is owed four days and is put off until after noon.
   580	
   581	**Objects and money.** Board purse unchanged: **a hundred and thirty-two earned; a hundred and eight in hand.** The Fallow hundred lies in Pike's box; no instruments were found; the posting (five strokes) is in Hesk's book. The crossbow, with **five bolts**, is with the crew; its spanning hook is in the mule's near-side pannier. One bolt lies on the Ring's floor. Six blankets returned, one a hand narrow. The rope is still owed.
   582	
   583	**Hounds.** Nine came; two are dead (one on the floor, one drawn off a hundred yards south of the stone, outside the line); **seven went north and south along the line's outside** on the night of the 96th and were not seen, tracked or heard again.
   584	
   585	**Pike's book and the wall.** Unchanged: seven lines; tenth; Teague nine up. The Fallow line has not been said. The two HOLD slips are unresolved on the page.
   586	
   587	**Who knows what.** The mechanism: the five. Oryn knows that he can do, inside a line, what no Path can; she saw Wind, a light, and heard an edge ring; she did not see the Shadow use and cannot attribute his arrival at Karis. Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln saw it. All six know that the registry's iron stands on the line, that maps were drawn with a blank there, and that the posting was a question which their coming out has answered. Nobody knows where the file is, what it says, or why. Nobody has said why the fragments answer inside.
   588	
   589	**Open threads.** The telling, on the table, owed that minute. What it cost her, if anything. A leaf in a loft to be fetched and read. *Later*, on Lira's side. Seven hounds. A report going west with six on it. An arm slung until the snow, and an ankle that nobody has mended. Eleven sheets not yet looked at. Two rings marked *guess*. The top gate of a round, eleven days north.
