+# TARGETED RECHECK r1 — Book 7, Movement 5 (chapters 31–37)
+
+## Verdict
+
+**CLOSE — manuscript.** The repair resolves every brief item, all nine repairable source-distance passages, the Reader Standard, the fragment/rule accounting, and the continuity handoffs. No manuscript line fix and no second author repair are needed.
+
+**Coordinator state cleanup before the CLOSED note:** two subordinate summaries in `STATE_LEDGER.md` still preserve superseded pre-repair facts. At `STATE_LEDGER.md:552`, Brom has “four finger-pads of each hand” and Cael is “bound by Karis, then by Oryn”; at `STATE_LEDGER.md:573`, Brom has “Eight finger-pads cut”. The binding coordinator rulings at 531–536, the surviving manuscript, the next-movement inheritance at 594–596, and `MOVEMENT-006.md:16–18` all have the repaired facts: **one hand, four finger-pads**, and **Karis's blanket strip remains on Cael's calf until Oryn removes it on the 99th**. This is coordinator bookkeeping, not a manuscript defect.
+
+## (1) Brief items
+
+Baseline checked with `diff -U0` against `state/movement-005/pre-repair-r1/`.
+
+### A. The weighing — RESOLVED
+
+- `chapter-36.md:183`: “the four names had been one name, which was *wrong*”. This replaces “nobody in that loft had called it wrong”.
+- `chapter-36.md:187`: “The right thing is to cross that yard tonight; or, failing that, to tell her in the morning before she has laid a hand on me. I know that.”
+- `chapter-36.md:225`: “it did not make the thing allowed”; the leaf “meant only” that he would pass both right doors “with his eyes open”.
+- `chapter-37.md:157–163`: “It would be right”; “That was the right road”; “he chose against it”; “a thing written down beforehand is only a thing done on purpose.”
+
+The diff makes all four required propositions explicit: all four companions called the act wrong; Cael knows refusal or prior disclosure is right; writing first makes the choice knowing rather than permitted; and neither desire, confession, nor the leaf supplies consent or forgiveness. Oryn's own naming, terms, and cost remain wholly for Movement 6.
+
+### B. Tracked passages — RESOLVED
+
+1. **B1, chapter 31 binding — RESOLVED.** The old “linen out” / healer's knee / advancing wrap / hard-knot chain is replaced by “It was Karis who moved first”; Brom's folded cuff becomes two pads; Oryn tears her shirt but “did not wind them herself”; Cael winds from elbow to wrist and tucks the end with “don't put a knot on the hurt.”
+2. **B2, chapter 32 throw — RESOLVED.** The neck-and-hindquarter lift is replaced by the knife-hilt lever: “He put the horn of the hilt in at the back of the jaw”; the released hound charges, Cael steps off-line, takes “one foreleg and a handful of hide”, and adds to its own motion. “He did that with his own two feet and nothing in them” keeps the throw fragment-free.
+3. **B3, chapter 32 second lock — RESOLVED.** Instead of a visible frontal hit held through shoulder, spine, and locked knees, the hound is behind him and hits “in the backs of the thighs”; his knees go, he pitches forward, and late Compression takes the blow down the one forearm already on the ground. The animal goes over his head and he rises behind it.
+4. **B4, chapter 33 hour — RESOLVED.** “for the whole of it he watched her face” becomes “he measured the hour by its oil”. Lira's hand supplies the changing measure; Seln notices Oryn's cost only after the hour: “grey to the lips” and “hair wet through, in this frost”.
+5. **B5, chapter 34 scene 3 — RESOLVED.** The scene enters after the throat treatment with Karis testing a drink. Brom first demonstrates the repaired hand by carrying the pan. Oryn visually names Cael's half-closed seam before contact; Lira forces the fourth read; it is taken at wrist and neck and stops at six; Oryn leaves Karis's blanket strip and knot in place.
+6. **B6, chapter 35 arrival — RESOLVED.** “It was the bowman who saw them first”; he waits at the east gate and sees only Lira's changed body. The steading's woman then comes from the house with a ladle, counts without an injury inventory, and says “Six. Well.” to the ladle.
+7. **B7, chapter 36 loft opening — RESOLVED.** The chapter now begins “He drew the ladder up himself”. Brom, oil/Karis, Lira, and Seln are placed only as their turns arrive, rather than in the source-order opening tableau.
+8. **B8, chapter 37 “along, not down” — RESOLVED.** The water/channel image becomes a joiner testing a plank. Cael first recognizes the unevenness made by Oryn's raw heel; only afterward does he find her road beat. “This one limped” makes personhood arrive through irregularity before cadence.
+
+The tenth original tracking finding, Brom's hand at `chapter-34.md:129–133`, is protected and remains verbatim rather than being treated as repairable prose.
+
+### C. The aftermath told once — RESOLVED
+
+- `chapter-32.md:313` now defers the body count: “Four of the six were hurt, and he would have the count of that by lamplight.”
+- `chapter-33.md:37` replaces the repeated injury inventory with “she'll have each of those from the one that it belongs to.”
+- `chapter-33.md:59–75` removes the second bill-by-bill accounting from the hour while retaining the dead forearm needed for the lantern action.
+- The night log remains the one complete accounting: its ten written lines yield twelve uses, and “With the ford, thirteen.”
+- `chapter-34.md:203` no longer repeats arm/throat/fingers/leg/number.
+- `chapter-35.md:53–59` keeps a short second-night state and the required deployment total without replaying the maps, stake, or body catalogue.
+
+The medical consequences, acts of care, bolt count, Seln's maps, night log, and required thirteen all remain.
+
+### D. Rhythm — RESOLVED
+
+The diff shows the requested joins in `chapter-36.md:75–109` and `chapter-37.md:101–129`, while new action and moral-weighing passages break at genuine turns. Reproduced movement metrics are mean **13.70**, sentences of at least forty words **4.0%**, and **986.3 words per scene**, all within the brief's movement bands. Chapter 33's long-sentence share is **3.4%**, down from 5.6% before repair. Chapter 32's individual mean remains 14.74 and is not a finding: the brief explicitly permitted the fight/run to stand provided the movement-level targets held.
+
+### Direct source-distance recheck
+
+I reopened source chapters 11–13 and compared the repaired passages by content and order, not wording alone.
+
+1. **Chapter 31 binding — RESOLVED.** Source 11:69 proceeds linen → healer's knee/weight → winding → hard knot. Current 31:295–315 proceeds Karis pressure → cuff pads → Oryn's raised knee supporting the arm → Cael's reverse-direction winding → tucked end/no knot.
+2. **Chapter 32 throw — RESOLVED.** Source 11:119–121 uses neck and hind leg, lifts the rear, turns through the throw, and lands the hound south. Current 32:129–139 first levers the mouth open, lets the hound launch anew, steps off-line, and redirects its forward motion by foreleg and hide.
+3. **Chapter 32 second lock — RESOLVED.** Source 11:147–151 is a low frontal strike taken on the shoulder by a standing frame. Current 32:253–263 is an unseen rear strike to the thighs that collapses Cael and is grounded through the planted forearm. Required lock, late Compression, bill, and westward escape remain without the source chain.
+4. **Chapter 33 hour — RESOLVED.** Source 11:201 watches Oryn and reads her cost directly during the treatment. Current 33:59–75 measures oil and Lira's grip; Seln supplies Oryn's physical cost afterward at 127.
+5. **Chapter 34 throat — RESOLVED.** Source 12:51–57 narrates hands, count, still treatment, swallow, colour change, then prognosis. Current 34:113–125 enters after the treatment with Karis already drinking and gives the prognosis retrospectively.
+6. **Chapter 34 calf — RESOLVED.** Source 12:81–95 removes dried cloth, washes, brackets the calf, fails the count, names the rule, notices closure, and rebinds. Current 34:141–177 visually identifies closure under an existing edge first; Lira then forces a wrist-and-neck read; Oryn refuses repetition and leaves Karis's strip untouched.
+7. **Chapter 35 arrival — RESOLVED.** Source 13:3–7 puts the steading's woman at the entry and runs count/injury inventory before “Six. Well.” Current 35:283–303 gives the east-gate bowman the first recognition, moves the woman from house to step, and removes the inventory.
+8. **Chapter 36 loft opening — RESOLVED.** Source 13:35–37 inventories oil, Lira, Brom, Karis, and Seln in that order. Current 36:3–39 enters on the ladder and distributes people when they speak in a different order.
+9. **Chapter 37 “along” — RESOLVED.** Source 13:157–161 uses stream/channel → length → regular road pace → person keeping time. Current 37:21–31 uses plank/edge → asymmetric pressure caused by a raw heel → beat afterward → “This one limped.”
+
+**New tracking: none.** The rewritten material introduces no new same-content/same-order chain. The automated overlap check also reports **0 unprotected shared runs of eight or more words**; its 38 matches are protected.
+
+## (2) Continuity
+
+### Calendar, entry, exit, and handoff
+
+The movement enters at sunset on day 96 exactly where chapter 30 leaves the six at the Ring's eastern lip. It crosses the line that night, uses day 97 for treatment and mapping, day 98 for Oryn's crossings, reaches Thornwater on day 99, and ends during the long reading on day 100. This agrees with `BOOK_MAP.md`, the Movement 4 closing state, the binding After Movement 5 rulings, and the openings of Movements 6–8. No season/month wording, new name, or reserved truth leaks onto the page.
+
+### Count and capability rules
+
+No fragment use was added or removed by the repair. The night log at `chapter-33.md:199–217` accounts for Iron read (1), Shadow (1), first Wind (1), Pressure (1), Ember (1), Blade (1), Anchor (1), Storm's three lanes (3), second Wind (1), and Compression (1): **twelve in the Ring**. With the ford, the total is **thirteen**. The two private noon tests remain separately acknowledged and excluded at 227–229. The tenth fragment is acquired only on day 100; it is not part of the Ring deployment sum.
+
+Every use obeys `STATE_LEDGER.md` §2: Iron reads ground only; Shadow removes notice for ten strides; Wind bursts and imposes its fixed one-count landing lock both times; Pressure declares into the ground; Ember is one point on the knife; Blade supplies an edge; Anchor perceives fixed points without fixing one; Storm spends three discrete air lanes and loses the ground read while held; Compression arrives at contact and sends force into the ground. Shadow's seal also holds on the page at `chapter-32.md:111–125`: the four informed companions have sightlines, while Brom and the box screen Oryn, whose attention remains on Karis/Lira. She sees where Cael arrives, not where he begins, and cannot attribute the use.
+
+### Bodies and follow-on facts
+
+- **Brom:** one injured hand and the pads of four fingers everywhere; the three restored protected runs at `chapter-34.md:129–133` are exact; `chapter-36.md:17` says one hand is pale. His own “The hundredth” preserves the no-string restriction through day 99.
+- **Oryn's failed Cael reads:** chapter 20's first reading stops at five (`20:327–341`); chapter 22 contains the second rib reading and third wrist/neck reading, followed by “That's three times” (`22:53–73`); Lira forces the fourth in chapter 34 at wrist/neck, stopping at six (`34:157–175`); the pre-long-reading surface count reaches ten and is explicitly “the fifth time” (`36:263–269`). “I don't say a finding four times to a patient and change it on the fifth” is numerically exact. The Movement 3 stop at five is not contradicted by the fourth attempt stopping at six.
+- **Cael's calf:** Karis binds it with the grey blanket strip at `chapter-33.md:147–151`; Oryn says “Don't take it off” and leaves Karis's knot at `chapter-34.md:147–177`; she removes that same knot in the Thornwater yard at `chapter-35.md:329`. Oryn never binds it.
+- **Brom's folded cuff:** at `chapter-31.md:303` it is torn into two pads and spent on Lira's arm; `chapter-33.md:9` identifies the two cuff pads in the removed dressing.
+- **Bowman:** he waits at the east gate and takes off his cap at `chapter-35.md:285–289`.
+- **Lantern oil:** four fingers when lit (`chapter-33.md:61`), three after the hour (`33:185`), one in the loft (`36:19`).
+
+These repaired facts agree with the closed manuscript and `MOVEMENT-006.md:16–18`. The two stale ledger summaries identified under the verdict do not govern over the binding rulings or surviving prose and should be corrected administratively.
+
+### Protected text, knowledge, and reserved facts
+
